  "minimum_interface": [
    "Create a source-bound rewind anchor at pre-action P while the session cache is exclusively checked out: exact prefix IDs/hash, policy/runtime identity, session epoch and layer inventory/window metadata; clone only sliding-layer P tails and save P.",
    "At stop, operate only on an exclusively owned B1 cache (or the existing stop-time extracted row); crop each full DynamicLayer to P and transfer saved sliding keys/values plus cumulative_length=P. Do not call uniform Cache.crop on an already-evicted sliding layer.",
    "Retain/store the rewound cache under the original exact P prefix, not the raw decoded suffix. Reuse only if the next rendered/canonical prompt strictly extends that exact P and the same policy/runtime/epoch; otherwise drop it and prefill fresh.",
    "Treat sliding backup as consumed ownership on restoration; release it on cancellation, stale epoch, exception or fresh-prefill fallback. For batched decode preserve per-session anchors before packing, and never mutate a shared packed cache as though it were one B1 session."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This proves one real FP32 CPU causal non-shared tiny Gemma4 boundary, not Unsloth/NF4/CUDA/31B throughput or memory savings.",
    "DynamicLayer.crop makes a view: immediately after cropping, its actual backing storage still holds the longer raw tail; the subsequent cache update/cat materializes a new prefix-plus-canonical tensor. No instant physical memory-shrink claim.",
    "DynamicSlidingWindowLayer.keys may itself be a view into a longer prefill tensor; the measured sliding backup is a clone of only window-1 entries, so its storage is actually bounded rather than retaining that larger base tensor.",
    "If history canonicalization changes any token before P, this P anchor is unusable; strict extension must fail closed to fresh prefill. No inferred canonical prefix reuse.",
    "Existing batched stop-time extraction can already copy a full B1 row out of the packed cache. This proposal avoids an additional full pre-action backup; it does not erase the existing extraction cost.",
    "No sampled behavior/reference probabilities were rewritten, no default sampler/trainer source changed, no optimizer/GPU/download/heldout/new test or script."
